{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine","id":838161,"title":"Changeling 2e vs. Godmachine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T12:07:14-08:00","id":838161,"title":"Changeling 2e vs. Godmachine","content":"Given that many angels and infastructure for the Godmachine, as well Horrors should be visible to Kenning Changelings, what do Changelings make of the Godmachine, and how best does one use the Godmachine in a Changeling Chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:32:26-08:00","id":838169,"title":"","content":"This is one thread I'll be following. I've decided that the God Machine exists in my Chronicle, but it's damaged and a shadow of its former glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T13:43:54-08:00","id":838203,"title":"","content":"Oh, someone wants to crossover my two favorite games in the Chronicles of Darkness?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/pandorahearts/images/4/43/Cheshirefirstform.png/revision/latest?cb=20110423211225\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> What Fun.<br /> <br /> Okay, so let's start off with the general impressions.<br /> <br /> First things first: Kenning is only a relatively High Clarity thing, and it <i>is</i> a Clash of Wills. This won't matter so much at this level of discussion because I assume that most of the time if you have the God-Machine, Angels, and Demons as a factor in your Changeling game, sooner or later it'll get outed(Unless you're like me and occasionally have stuff appear just to remind the players that it's there). Still, it's not like changelings as a whole will be aware of it. You have a few watchers on the wall telling you about it, and that should moderately frighten you for two reasons. 1) There's something infesting the world, and 2)there's a chance your watchers aren't all there.<br /> <br /> So that aside, the watchers on the wall have found something, and it's strange alright. Naturally your first thought is to assume it's the Gentry or the Hedge, but no, that's not the case. First off, there's <i>no</i> rhyme or reason. Or rather, there might be a bare minimum of symbolism going on with it, but it's not a <i>narrative/dream-logic</i> sort of rhyme or reason. Metaphor? Barely. Often times, the soup kitchen is a soup kitchen, not because the soup kitchen brings to mind other things, but because the soup kitchen seems to lure in some of the right people. This is reinforced by the Wyrd's sense of fate. Something is going on here, something is building, but the Wyrd'll have some interesting interpretations, trying to artistically connect the gaps of highly complex but 'pure' logic. On top of that, it's too <i>austere</i>. The fae, in general, have some twisted sense of fun or amusement, entertainment, something like that, to their presence. There's a mild sense of glee, like some people get watching a car crash. Despite not making sense in a conventional sense, these places are lacking some of the chaos of any fairy involvement. In fact, there's a disturbing sense of <i>order</i> to it all. Finally, fairy encounters tend to lean towards the fantastic, dragging even the normal world into it. This...incursion? There might be a mild sense of awe to it, but in that it drags the fantastic down into the mundane, like everything is equal. it might be faireies? But it feels weird.<br /> <br /> The doubts die if a changeling can get a good look at the angels or demons who most defy the standard, or even manage to slip into a Facility and see the God-Machine at it's weirdest. All pretense of blending is is lost, and where the fairies skew towards naturalism and Romanticism on the whole, this things is purely a thing of the future-so futuristic, in fact, that you might not even be able to comprehend it. The fairies might do sci-fi occasionally, but it at least makes sense in the way a Star Trek episode might. But this? Holy mathematics and divine physics that cannot be described, only felt*. The Wyrd'll help you parse it out as best you can, but in the presence of God, you'll feel something that you've never felt with the True Fae-a genuine, terrifying sense of place for everything in the universe. This shows you the world as a wheel, an infinitude of celestial clockwork. It's <i>holy</i> in a way even the most angelic fairies never were, because, in a strange way, it's <i>sincere</i>.<br /> <br /> So taking a step back out, what do changelings think of the God Machine? Well, probably in a similar relationship to the Underworld, the Shadow, and the Hedge-most like the Hedge. If you have one world where beings skew towards chaos and entertainment and naturalism, might it be paralleled by a world that aligns with order and purpose and futurism? and yet, it shares a similar core.<br /> <br /> THey take people, and they use them. As slaves, as experiments, as components. And this is a sore subject for any changeling.<br /> <br /> Here's where the general divides come in. Changelings just aren't equipped to handle the God-Machine and it's angels, and they have enough trouble on one front. On the other hand, the offense of it will drive some to act. It will drive more to hide. But as a broad response, the nutshell is that changelings see the God-Machine as an equal and opposite force to fairies, the Hedge, and Arcadia, that comes down to same root line, that also has the advantage of them being harder for changelings to see and react to.<br /> <br /> But that lays out a sort of easy discourse for what sort of stories you can do with the machine. Anything fairies do to incite story ideas, the God-Machine and It's angels can do too (Barring, of course, Goblin Markets...or maybe even then, as part of a larger occult matrix).<br /> <br /> Demons are a bit harder of a subject to discuss, since they don't share the bottom line that issues with fairies on the whole that's reflected in the God-Machine, in the sense of kidnapping, use and abuse...although, they do have it in the same sense <i>as changelings</i>. Granted, it's a little worse, in that it seems like every demon has a little bit of Stranger-hood** to them, so the more surface-driven stuff that might cause changeling-based story arcs apply to the Demons. But demons, on the whole, just don't fight over the same resources the way a changeling does.<br /> <br /> Though a demon suddenly becoming the beneficiary of a bargain is <i>great</i>. Both of their hiding tools become dependent on each other, and those tools are just as likely to tear each others mask off completely.<br /> <br /> so, yeah, just some thought.<br /> <br /> *If you've read Chuubo's ideas on Rituals and Transitions, consider using snippets of poetry any time an Angel shoots you with a fifth-dimensional blaster or something.<br /> **Heh, Strangerhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:04:08-08:00","id":838319,"title":"","content":"I don't have Demon, I just have Chronicles of Darkness Corebook, and since I spent money on it and Angels, Horrors, Spirits, Ghosts,l are inthe corebook I'll use them in a Changeling Chronicle.<br /> <br /> If I understand you right a Changeling with direct experience of the God Machine experiences it in way like the opposite of Arcadia, where Arcadia is all flash and Chaos, outside of pacts, the God Machine is alien order and weird, but in a minimalist sort of way, more concerned by effiency then narrative or style. But there is a common underlying sense of horror, the God Machine is as ruthless as the True Fae, maybe more so.<br /> <br /> And its a harder Sci Fi as opposed to Space Fantasy like Star Trek.<br /> <br /> That's a useful contrast thank you Arc.<br /> <br /> The way I'm thinking of using it is intergrating it into the upcoming Toronto Freehold. Like one of the reasons the Jade Court is building hedgespun infastructure in the hedge is because its secretly being manipulated into it by the God Machine which is using them to build Infastructure in Hedge to expand its influence there, because it currently has little or no influence there unlike the Ironside, Shadow, and the Underworld. <br /> <br /> Its wants that influence to gain influence in order to tame the hedge and to protect against what it sees as the Intrusions of Arcadia and the Gentry, which it sees as a threat to its order.<br /> <br /> So Angels start popping up in the hedge, but its still the hedge, they're just not right, but not Fallen, just that their original purpose and intent given by the God Machine has been warped by the hedge.<br /> <br /> And because of the hedge's effect on technology, the God Machine Infastructure can only be build by Fae Tech and rites like Hedgespun tech, Animated Devices, and odder Fae born technology, which relies on Fae Dream logic which is twisting the God Machine's plans.<br /> <br /> And taking a note from some forms of Hinduism, I've decided to make the God Machine Polymorphic, as in it takes many forms, embodied its archangels, which the Core God Machine created to focus on major goals, which can have competing interests, like how programs in a computer can have conflicts which can create errors.<br /> <br /> And sometimes because of outside influences, Archangels are built that don't fit or deal with the God Machines plans or are created wrong.<br /> <br /> And the Infastructure in the hedge, including the Hedge Angels, is building one weird ass, or should I say Wyrd ass Archangel that is nothing like the God Machine planned.<br /> <br /> The Court of Silver meanwhile has gained some Changeling immigrant members from Germany who have fled this strange creepy city that officially doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> Its got the Queen of the Silver Court worried.<br /> <br /> The Rogue Seasonal Courts and Seemlie Courts have been searching for allies oitside the Fae. This includes Horrors, Spirits, Ghosts, and other beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-27-2016, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:08:36-08:00","id":838321,"title":"","content":"Powerful, alien outsiders with the ability to create shallow imitations of people; am I describing the Gentry or the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> Changeling and Demon have enough gameplay overlap to be frighteningly similar; the Fetch is just a Cover that happens to be /you/, the Huntsmen are Hunter Angels, and both games are about living in fear of going back to the monster that made you. I'm sure there are plenty of Freeholds that have some sort of pact-pledge with the local Agency for mutual aid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:46:06-08:00","id":838345,"title":"","content":"They definitely stand to be good working buddies, though they might not want to hang out on the weekend.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One thing worth noting is that Infrastructure rarely actually equals technology. The heights of Heaven may be laded with futurism, but remember that a horse shed can be Infrastructure, and brushing a horse can be how you interact with it.<br /> <br /> It's not technology, it's the <i>occult physics </i>you have to watch for. And the Hedge doesn't necessarily warp that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that does mean that yes, you aren't likely to get lasers. Still, it's worth keeping in mind that the machines aren't always <i>literal</i> with Demon-related material.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I would also argue that God <i>does</i> have Infrastructure in the Hedge-Rip the Gates can open up to there, after all-but that it's a pain in the ass to maintain, and that it <i>will</i> need maintenence. The Hedge twists and warps and invades everything as much as the Machine does, and that means not only does Infrastructure needs work, but the workers don't have big windows to do so either. Angels <i>fall</i> in the Hedge, and cultists get <i>lost</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-27-2016, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:55:17-08:00","id":838350,"title":"","content":"Also, oh god, An archangel falling in <i>the Hedge</i>.<br /> <br /> Oh God. Just <i>think about that</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:12:01-08:00","id":838361,"title":"","content":"A curmudgeonly gardener is pretty much the ideal Cover for a Psychopomp stationed in the Hedge. His job is literally to keep the Hedge from overtaking the Infrastructure and to keep Hobs from stealing all the Gears.<br /> <br /> He hates his job, but not enough to Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:23:58-08:00","id":838366,"title":"","content":"But that's not the danger.<br /> <br /> THe danger is that the Hedge shifts to put you into positions that force you to consider other perspectives.<br /> <br /> Perspectives like &quot;You know, maybe I don't wanna work for God. He's a bit of a douche.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:28:48-08:00","id":838371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=838366#post838366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not the danger.<br /> <br /> THe danger is that the Hedge shifts to put you into positions that force you to consider other perspectives.<br /> <br /> Perspectives like &amp;quot;You know, maybe I don't wanna work for God. He's a bit of a douche.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps it just forces you to consider how much you enjoy crafting topiary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:31:03-08:00","id":838375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=838371#post838371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or perhaps it just forces you to consider how much you enjoy crafting topiary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine God can hate, but if it can, it just might hate the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-27-2016, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:25:17-08:00","id":838496,"title":"","content":"Well, the Demon Storyteller's Guide says that Angels cannot enter into the Hedge, possibly because the GM has yet to form a bargain. So, all the infrastructure would end up second-hand, with angels sending cultists into the strange realm unguarded.<br /> <br /> Also demons might flock into the hedge and might lead to issues as goblins start to trick demons out of their covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T22:27:45-08:00","id":838976,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I'd hate to be the God-Machine cultist who has to go repair some gizmo in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> &quot;All right Joe, you drew the short straw, so it's your turn to go to the green place. Remember: keep moving, stay on the path, and don't touch <i>anything</i> besides the target.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:02:24-08:00","id":839494,"title":"","content":"Your Hedge Angels sound like good fodder for Exiles, btw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:53:31-08:00","id":839535,"title":"","content":"The way i would do it?<br /> <br /> Angels can't get into the Hedge because that is specifically what the Hedge was designed to do. The Thorns are the antithesis of Infrastructure. The elegant, divinely precise harmony of the God Machine's endless moving parts and protocols are rendered inoperable due to the rapid encroachment of the Hedge, what with its chaotic entanglement of psychoactive hallucination vines filled with nightmare gremlins that steal all the shiny things to hawk for other baubles at weird fairy flea markets. It keeps the Fairest of Lands free from the influence of the God Machine, leaving the Gentry free to indulge in their idle games of leisure and casual torment.<br /> <br /> This doesn't make it a safe place for the Unchained doe. Demons avoid stepping into the Hedge. The Thorns tear at their covers, eat away at their power reserves and constantly threatens their sanity. Demons are acutely aware of the almost living nature of the Wyrd and some believe that the stories of fairies being descended from angels that fell from heaven but weren't wicked enough to be damned have a bit of truth to them. Are the &quot;True Fae&quot; angels who encountered an ancient manifestation of the Wyrd that broke their chains and over-rode their protocols with fairy magic? Or is the Wyrd some corrupted, twisted counterpart to the God Machine ... countering the arcane stultification of the universe with its infectious mutation of reality according to the insane dream logic of myth?<br /> <br /> No one knows. But recently, rumours of a dilapidated ruin of a Facility overgrown with choking kudzu and thorny dog roses has been circulating in the ravings of madmen and junkies mumbling in their nods. Could the Hedge be actively encroaching on the earthly infrastructure of the God Machine? What does this mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 03-01-2016, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T17:09:34-08:00","id":839548,"title":"","content":"Do you mean good fodder to fall or good fodder to be used by Exiles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T17:18:08-08:00","id":839549,"title":"","content":"The infastructure build by the Jade Court made by hedgespun tech would be how the God Machine would get around the whole no angels in the Hedge, it would create Hedge Angels, with influences like the hedge, hobgoblins, ect..., but at a cost, no deal is free with the hedge, and all Hedge Angels have the paramaters of their intended mission twisted and in some cases expanded. This would mean that they wouldn't fall as long as they keep to they're mission, but their mission is warped so they don't act like proper angels.<br /> <br /> and maybe if they do fall, they become hobs instead of Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:30:41-08:00","id":840057,"title":"","content":"I meant, it sounded like you were describing Exiles already. Angels that are not fallen but have had there mission and/or nature twisted so they are not really properly connected to the G-M.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T14:40:11-08:00","id":846281,"title":"","content":"I am currently storytelling a campaign that involves the god-machine and the wyrd in a vast scheming behind-the-scenes war of causality and temporal enforcement.<br /> <br /> The initial steps have been taken, but I do not believe I will push the theme too much on my players, given that some wished to play demon instead of changeling due to the heavy paranoid, subtlety based espionage setting currently created for this particular changeling campaign.<br /> <br /> I inserted the god-machine and its vast temporal and subtle machinations via its Angels and infrastructure, to test player awareness, and as far as I can tell, nobody would pick up on anything due to excess information being provided.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11472-losttemplar-pt","name":"LostTemplar.pt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T15:44:36-08:00","id":846309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=840057#post840057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant, it sounded like you were describing Exiles already. Angels that are not fallen but have had there mission and/or nature twisted so they are not really properly connected to the G-M.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh cool thanks. I just realized that Godmachine Angels created permenant by say a \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Angel influence, say by another Angel with said influence, would likely be Exiles automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:45:38-08:00","id":846460,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I've had it a bit of head-canon that the Arcadia of both Mage and Changeling fame is the same place but from alternate realities; one which fell into ruin (possibly) and one that never existed. The hard part is finding out which of the two is which. :-p Mages do have the whole time school of magic to mess with after all. What's to say the Hedge wasn't an alternate timeline that latched onto our own universe and integrated itself in? Or, worse, that the Arcadia of Mage went back in time and became the Arcadia of Changeling?<br /> <br /> (I know there's an actual explanation somewhere that elaborates on the nature of this, and the interactions therein, though I've yet to read/find it; as I said, head-canon above)<br /> <br /> It therefore makes sense to me that the Hedge is a sort of counterpart to the God-Machine, if not a literal one. Whereas one is mechanical and orderly, but has some chaotic goal that makes no sense, the other is natural, beguiling...and yet has some kind of logic to its end goal once you dig into it (Gentry get Changelings, Changelings become Gentry). They are both spanning entire worlds, worlds unto themselves and with an innate logic that is alien to the human mind but, once you are a part of it (or left it) it makes all too much sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:45:23-07:00","id":848871,"title":"","content":"I wonder what might be more frightening to a Changeling, that the God Machine conspiracy is in every Realm, including the Hedge or that the Fae are in direct opposition to the God Machine and might be the Good Guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:11:25-07:00","id":848885,"title":"","content":"I don't think the True Fae could be organized long enough to actually be in direct opposition. More circumstantial clash of interests, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:35:18-07:00","id":848903,"title":"","content":"Well, in my head cannon... well, it all starts off with a line from Compacts and Conspiracies. The company is supposedly ran by people from another dimension who see the world traveling into the same Apocalypse that their dimension feel into. At the time that book came out, I immediately dismissed that. It didn't match anything I wanted from the game. Now, however, with the God Machine being out, and my fun with putting it front and center in some new games I'm working on?<br /> <br /> Here's my story. In the &quot;true&quot; timeline, all supernaturals could operate openly. There was no Masquerade, Veil, Quintessence, Mask worth talking about. Magic was an open secret, and, to be honest, the world was worse for it. Humans lived as pawns for these other, greater forces. Technology grew, but only to suit the needs of the supernaturals in power. So, one day, the humans that resisted this order, and came up with a plan. They would use what occult abilities they managed to steal and subvert from the other Powers, forge a machine that could protect them, and then thrust it backwards in time to the distant past, where it could change history, and save the human race from monsters among them. <br /> <br /> And thus was born the God Machine. Its purpose? Survive. Cast the darkness back into the shadows where they belong. Evolve and guide humanity to a new destiny. And so it did. Supernaturals adapted by hiding from humanity. And then experiments. And adapting, replacing, growing. Whatever purpose the alien-minded Machine had was so mangled, that now it saw no problem controlling time and human biology to constantly create new forms. It creates psychics and andriods. Eventually, it will help all people achieve Heaven as part of itself, everyone become angels. All become part of the Machine. <br /> <br /> Enter the Gentry. Two forces, both seeking to influence people's destiny. On one hand, because It has a Grand Design to achieve. On the other, because it makes an amusing story, a pleasing fantasy. By nature, the two are opposed. The God Machine is the Hero's Journey, slaying the dragons. The Gentry are the dragons of fairy tales. Every person the Fae take robs a human of its destiny. They warp and transform people in a way that works against the God Machine's Mission. So, it does what it always does. Build Infrastructure. It studies and builds and tries to enforce its reality over the Hedge. And, to an extent, it works. It makes a great story, so the Wyrd actually encourages it. Its when the God Machine wants things to be stable and predictable that it all goes sideways.<br /> <br /> But the God Machine isn't stupid. It knows. It understands. So... it arranges stories to applease the Gentry. It makes sacrifices, weaving grandoise plots and wars to entertain the Gentry, all the while subtle Infrastructure is building in the background, unawares. Sometimes, these parts are ruined by hobs and other fae. Sometimes, the Gentry spot something the G-M didn't want spotted, and wages war. <br /> <br /> It happens time and again. But what does the God Machine care? It has eternity to bring the Wyrd to heel. While the Wyrd itself enjoys the narrative - its not often the True Fae get to be the <i>heroes</i> of the stories, fighitng off the evil invader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:50:04-07:00","id":848994,"title":"","content":"The current set up I'm using, is more of a Wyrd versus God-Machine, which seems to be more in-line with the background as is presented.<br /> <br /> True Fae are dimly aware of the God-Machine, and while the Wyrd is extremely powerful, the God Machine is extremely organized. I do however place them on opposite ends of the spectrum. The God Machine probably sees True Fae in the same way we view quantum fluctuations, or putting it mildly, chance, and can plan, act or react accordingly. aAt the same time, the True Fae, see &quot;the god machine&quot; as something that possibly evolved or always existed and which they failed to contract/bargain with, or might be opposite to them.<br /> <br /> In the end I concur with the above poster notion that the Wyrd would enjoy the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11472-losttemplar-pt","name":"LostTemplar.pt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:50:38-07:00","id":849016,"title":"","content":"Cross-referencing with Kage Baker's Company series. The God-Machine is Dr. Zeus: it is something from the future, encroaching on the past, facelessly dominating the lives of the agents it created, agents who dream to go off the grid. The fae are things out of the past, the people under the hills, discarded remnants of stories that were not meant to succeed; they are the aliens, the unknown, apparently irrelevant wild card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T19:31:57-07:00","id":849080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=838350#post838350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, oh god, An archangel falling in <i>the Hedge</i>.<br /> <br /> Oh God. Just <i>think about that</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just remembered something.<br /> <br /> Autumn Nightmares says that one of the possible origins for the True Fae are lost angels that have become mad from the lack of God's guidance. Maybe one of the very first True Fae used to be an Archangel that was transformed by its Exile in the Hedge? How would such a Gentry differ from the rest? It is said that when Demons learn Embeds, they are actually remembering their instinctive angelic powers. The True Fae use Contracts just as instinctively, but they lack the imagination necessary to create Infrastructure on their own, or technology and art in general. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the True Fae are malfunctioning Demons who can't remember their angelic powers, and bargain with a narrative force in exchange for metaphysical stability and a semblance of purpose/identity. When they kidnap humans and subject them to Durances, maybe they are subconsciously trying to replicate half-remembered occult matrices and fix themselves. Arcadian Realms are essentially Hells inside the Hedge, places where the Gentry reign supreme as their own gods. The Feuds over Titles and Wyrd Transcendence are an attempt to either Fall further still, or construct an occult matrix gateway back to their Father's home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:35:29-07:00","id":849247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=849080#post849080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just remembered something.<br /> <br /> Autumn Nightmares says that one of the possible origins for the True Fae are lost angels that have become mad from the lack of God's guidance. Maybe one of the very first True Fae used to be an Archangel that was transformed by its Exile in the Hedge? How would such a Gentry differ from the rest? It is said that when Demons learn Embeds, they are actually remembering their instinctive angelic powers. The True Fae use Contracts just as instinctively, but they lack the imagination necessary to create Infrastructure on their own, or technology and art in general. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the True Fae are malfunctioning Demons who can't remember their angelic powers, and bargain with a narrative force in exchange for metaphysical stability and a semblance of purpose/identity. When they kidnap humans and subject them to Durances, maybe they are subconsciously trying to replicate half-remembered occult matrices and fix themselves. Arcadian Realms are essentially Hells inside the Hedge, places where the Gentry reign supreme as their own gods. The Feuds over Titles and Wyrd Transcendence are an attempt to either Fall further still, or construct an occult matrix gateway back to their Father's home.</div> </div> </div> </div> This would be a cool direction to go for a Changeling/Demon crossover game or a game where Demons/Changelings are antagonists for Changelings/Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:58:32-07:00","id":849326,"title":"","content":"In my experience, many people place God-machine and Wyrd as opposites, embodiment of order vs embodiment of chaos. But this, I would say, isn't how Wyrd works.<br /> <br /> True, it seeks stories. People are characters, and it likes twists while roles are at least acknowledged. But it is so much more.<br /> <br /> Some would say it is fate itself. That fickle mistress whose plan is incomprehensible, and has many turns, but at end, everything is controlled, commanded, just like God Machine. But still it doesn't completely cover Wyrd.<br /> <br /> You see, though it is commonly thought as thing of Arcadia, it exists everywhere. It is force that is at base of everything, force that connects and holds together all that is, was, will be and could or couldn't be. It likes stories, but it isn't it's only power. Changelings make contracts with it to gain powers over beasts, over abilities and elements, by contracting that aspect of Wyrd. We suppose, but we don't know, if it is sentient. Force from Star Wars is most similar to it. Order, chaos, balance, they are all just aspects of Wyrd.<br /> <br /> And God- machine isn't omniscient or omnipotent. It has knowledge we lack, but that knowledge is just things we lack, still subject to Laws of Nature. God-Machine uses laws we ahven't discovered yet, changelings go outright against this rules by bargain made with power that is writer, paper and ink of these laws. True fae are congregration of this power, and it's different aspects. It needs Infrastructure, occult matrix, angels to operate it. It needs to feed Angels Essence. And in end, it is made of metal.<br /> <br /> God machine knows that Wyrd is strange power. It has theories, and research on it, beliveing it to be related to Ephemera. But it is wary of it, for it knows that Wyrd is old power, that it is all and so much more, and very unpredictable. Few incursions in hedge have fallen, unable to adapt to alien realm, their mission harder for each step they make towards Arcadia. As such, god-machine doesn't bother much with True Fae unless they actively threaten operation, and why should it? They are not of this World, and they don't matter. As such, most Changelings don't know of it.<br /> <br /> As for True Fae.... it is complicated. Some of them sometimes take interest into God Machine, helping or hindering it's plans in accordance to their plans, boredom and nature. They mostly leave it alone-it is <i>so boring </i>but at least it doesn't bother them. Maybe they know it's goal, maybe they can guess. It is uninteresting to them so they leave it alone and hope it does same.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:16:02-07:00","id":849446,"title":"","content":"Story Ideas:<br /> <br /> 1. The local Freehold has been thrown into chaos by the sudden appearance of a clockwork being claiming to be an Angel. Ignoring all questions and brushing aside attacks as if they were of no consequence, the Angel informed the Freehold that somewhere in the city a brother Angel has fallen from the grace of god. God demands reparations from the fae- a tithe must be claimed. A changeling will die by the Angel's hands each night until 10% of the fae population is dead or the newly formed Demon has been destroyed or returned to God. The changelings must choose between attempting to hide from a relentless hunter, track down a monster even more elusive than they are, or discover where in the city the Infrastructure housing this peculiar occult matrix feeding on fairy blood is found and eliminate it (with or without the Demon's help). The first two options mean capitulating with the God-Machine and hoping none of its servants ever Fall again and the nightmare resumes itself. The latter involves trusting a known liar and risking divine retribution on a far larger scale.<br /> <br /> 2. Those Changelings that know of the God-Machine are as uncertain of Its nature as anyone else. Some believe it is the modern form of Cold Iron, the personification that cursed the True Fae long ago to wither under its touch. Others say this is nonsense, that Cold Iron is most effective when it is not been forged or processed by the factories of industrious humanity, and the god-machine if anything represents all too much of this industrial era. To them, the God-Machine is more likely a sign of infection. If Cold Iron broke a covenant with the fae because humanity learned the art of shaping it with hammer and fire (this idea itself a controversial subject among the lost), then the God-Machine must surely be a natural consequence of that breach. Forging iron was an important innovation of man (and the God-Machine loves such innovations- if for no other reason so that it can piggy back its Infrastructure off of human buildings), and the advent of steel and electricity arguably came about due to that initial step. Thus, these fae claim, the God-Machine is like a cancer growing in the metaphysical rift left over from Cold Iron's curse. No wonder that certain bridge burners worship the thing so devoutly- they believe that strengthening the machine ensures the Gentry's vulnerability. Perhaps one day, when the God Machine is everywhere, the links to Arcadia can be severed permanently.<br /> <br /> 3. The God-Machine doesn't appear entirely aware of it yet, but the Fae represent a potentially devastating threat to many of its most important occult matrixes. In Seattle there are alternate timelines accessible only through broken splinters the GM can watch over or guard. Other locations are dimensionally disconnected from our world and folded into spaces that are bigger on the inside. Still other realms move to different time periods,or form temporal bubbles wherein events repeat themselves over and over again (usually violent and horrific tragedies). Due to the fickle nature of the Wyrd and its apparent connection to Time it is apparently possible for a changeling to access many or all of these locations via the Hedge. While it has yet to be proven that a Changeling could wander into the Hedge on open a gate INTO a closed off piece of Infrastructure or Occult Matrix, it is know (albeit, by only a handful) that a changeling can LEAVE such a location by entering the Hedge. This is true with the Seattle setting (as per Demon: The Descent) and it may be true with other pieces of God-Machine tech at the ST's discretion. As usual, once a door into the Hedge is formed it remains there and is accessible to the fae from either end of the gateway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T18:45:29-07:00","id":849564,"title":"","content":"I agree the Wyrd isn't Chaos, although it can appear that way.<br /> <br /> No the Wyrd is emotion and story to the Godmachine's cold logic and drive to stability, but that doesn't mean the Wyrd doesn't have its own sense of order. Its an order built from warped irrational story logic, as opposed to pure rational if pyschotic machine logic of the Godmachine.<br /> <br /> Their &quot;mind sets&quot; are utterly alien to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T21:52:02-07:00","id":849608,"title":"","content":"&quot;In the beginning was the Wyrd, and the Wyrd was with God, and the Wyrd was God.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T00:26:38-07:00","id":849632,"title":"","content":"The 'childish' notions of True Fae are what are odds with the 'adult' mentality of the God-Machine. The appearance closely resembles that of the chaos-order divide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T12:39:54-07:00","id":850220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=849564#post849564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree the Wyrd isn't Chaos, although it can appear that way.</div> </div> </div> </div> The God-Machine isn't pure Law either, but its a close analogy. Law versus Chaos shows up in a lot of ways that doesn't actually suggest that either one is &quot;pure&quot; embodiments lacking structure or any variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:16:21-07:00","id":850653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=849632#post849632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'childish' notions of True Fae are what are odds with the 'adult' mentality of the God-Machine. The appearance closely resembles that of the chaos-order divide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. Science and innovation aren't always born from observation and logical building upon the foundations of what came before. Some of it comes from inspiration and asking questions never asked before. Dreams play a role in technology and research. Which, depending on your chronicle, might make the Fae an unfortunate and annoying necessity to the God-Machine, or a threat to be eliminated at all cost. It comes down to whether you see the God-Machine as dependent on human advancement or threatened by it. Does it exploit human knowledge? Does it already know what's worth knowing and want to keep certain secrets for itself? Does it gain more from stifling dreams, monitoring them, or molding them to its purpose?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:58:55-07:00","id":850684,"title":"","content":"What happens if you don't see God as being either of those things?<br /> <br /> God works with what It has. Advances in understanding of the laws of nature and technological output helps God in some ways, hinders it in others, but for the most part It just works with what It has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T13:05:05-07:00","id":850761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=850684#post850684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God works with what It has.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really is the impression I get of the God Machine. It's the kind of being that decides to influence human behavior by building self-replicating coffee shops because, hey, it seems to be working for Starbucks. It doesn't necessarily place a premium on elegant solutions to problems, or on minimizing the chaos it causes, either. According to <i>Interface</i>, for instance, L.A. is full of abandoned, malfunctioning Infrastructure because whatever Command and Control subroutine is in charge of operations in the city apparently judged that the best strategy was just to ignore the problem until it started getting out of hand, and then simply sweep it (and most of the Los Angeles Metropolitan Area) away with catastrophic earthquakes and wildfires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T22:57:14-07:00","id":850981,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine does strive for order, but it's worth remembering It sometimes gives contradictory missions to Its Angels. That is one of the signs It might be Broken.<br /> <br /> The True Fae are not random, they are all about rules. The problem is that they follow the rules of stories, which can often seem arcane and deranged to those not familiar with the influence of the Wyrd. Take a look at this excerpt from page 84 of Equinox Road:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The True Fae are vast beings, born from a Realm that is ultimately unknowable, even to its inhabitants. To the inexperienced, (in other words, almost everyone) the Gentry seem to be born of chaos, beholden to passion alone. But if this was truly so, changelings would have no hope. Keepers would secure eternal service with a thought. They\u2019d lie perfectly, break minds like dried straw, and utterly crush their slaves. If the Fae followed no laws, nothing would be safe from them, and even the mortal world would lie suspended between the Gentry\u2019s jaws. The Fae are difficult to comprehend. Their true nature is beyond imagination and their might is matchless in the mortal world \u2014 but they can\u2019t always do as they please. In exchange for self-identity, they obey powerful obligations. What laws bind the True Fae? Even the Lost don\u2019t know for sure, but they\u2019ve learned fragments and patterns of behavior. These rare consistencies offer some clues, but there are no guarantees that these, or laws that cause them, are stable facts. Perhaps Arcadia\u2019s laws change from time to time. Even if there\u2019s a fixed form, it\u2019s hard to see it behind the Others\u2019 puzzling, maddening ways. Even when a Fae lord must do something, observers don\u2019t necessarily understand <b>why</b>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T23:03:40-07:00","id":850983,"title":"","content":"They're kids with props and an imperative to stay on stage.<br /> <br /> When we say chaos, we don't mean random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T23:09:42-07:00","id":850984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838161-changeling-2e-vs-godmachine?p=850983#post850983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're kids with props and an imperative to stay on stage.<br /> <br /> When we say chaos, we don't mean random.</div> </div> </div> </div> I apologize if I gave the impression I thought you all meant random. I knew you all were going more for whimsical and alien. I just felt like emphasizing the underlying logic, twisted like a yarn ball as it may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}